Here I am speeking about the WoW as a tool balanced between different
proficiency levels of players. This is noteworthy, because balancing a
powerful tool for various stages and various player proficiency levels
is not a trivially given property.

A newbie will not win with a fully charged WoW on level 1 but can take
advantage to "experiment" with usefulness of various wished objects.

An advanced player can use the Castle to his advantage to proceed to
areas with its own dangers for his experience, to obtain gear for
Gehennom, the Valley, the high demons, the Wizard; gear that he has
not yet foreseen to be necessary.

An advanced ascender might not even need the Castle WoW, because by
then he might as well ascend without any wishes in many cases; but he
may make certain aspects of his game less boring.

The probability for getting random wishes (or a random WoW) is also
very well balanced (or made sufficiently dangerous), and the Castle
location is very well chosen (WRT player proficiencies, as explained
above) for the single guaranteed set of wishes.

